# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
#
# The lint job rebuilds the worker (`sh src/web/wasm-worker/build.sh`) before
# the wasm-stage gates run, so comparing the checked-in binary against the
# working tree costs nothing extra and fails exactly when a commit changed the
# worker sources or their seeds without shipping the rebuilt artifact. That is
# how the branch went "js fallback" once already: plan 09 leaf 41 rewrote
# `engine_handler_precedence` and the precedence seed, the stale binary parsed
# the new seed into name-only rows, the browser worker's permutation assert
# threw at init, and every E2E spec gated on the "wasm worker" status fell back
# (issue #1138).
ci_gate check_wasm_worker_current
  stage wasm
  description "The checked-in WASM worker binary matches a rebuild of its sources."
  run "git diff --exit-code -- src/web/formal_ai_worker.wasm"
